*.exe
*.test
*.out
/oslo
/coverage.out
/bin
/build
/nimcache
/dist
/result
/.direnv
/.devbox
/.zig-cache
/zig-out
# Anchored `/target` only ever matched the workspace root, so a `cargo doc` or a rust-analyzer
# flycheck run inside `vendor/luna` left 7,000 files that `git add -A` swept into a release commit.
# Unanchored, so it matches at any depth.
target/
/.venv
/.pixi
/.micromamba
/.pytest_cache
/.ruff_cache
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
/.cargo/config.toml
compile_commands.json
.complog
.quickfix

# `src/data/` holds the structured pipeline: the value model, the planner and the tools.
#
# Un-ignored explicitly because a global ignore file may well exclude `data` directories — build
# output and datasets are usually called that — and one silently swallowing source is a bad way to
# find out. This repository's `data` is code.
!src/data/
!src/data/**

# **`src/` is source, whatever a global ignore thinks.** A `log` pattern in the user's global
# ignore file matched the *directory* `src/track/log/`, so `src/track/log/tests.rs` was never
# added — `make verify` passed locally and CI failed to compile on a file that was not in the
# repository. A directory has to be re-included before anything inside it can be.
!src/**/
!src/**

# **And `crates/`, for the same reason.** The rules above were written for a tree where all the
# source lived in `src/`; the six-crate split moved most of it to `crates/` and these
# re-inclusions did not follow. `crates/oslo-shell/src/data/custom.rs` then matched the global
# `**/data` rule, was never added, and CI failed to compile a file that existed on one machine —
# the same failure the comment above describes, in its new home.
#
# `vendor/` is deliberately not listed: it is somebody else's code and is added explicitly.
!crates/**/
!crates/**

# …but not a build directory inside one. The re-inclusion above is broad on purpose, and it undoes
# `target/` along with everything else: four `crates/oslo-shell/target/oslo-jump*/track.db` files
# from a test run were tracked this way. Listed after the re-inclusion, because last match wins.
crates/**/target/

# The other directories cargo builds from, so no global pattern can quietly empty one of them.
!bench/**
!tests/**
PLAN_AUDIT.md
